      "decision": "retainNote",
      "finding": "Even at zoom6 (scale 3.3, 2636x1974) on viewer page 528 (printed תקיא / 511), the lower vowel ink under initial vav in ונערְמוּ (y=886..914) is completely fused into the bottom of the vertical vav stem (y=824..887) with zero horizontal separation, forming a single continuous clubbed vertical mass. Unlike clean vav patah in וַיְהִי / וַיַּעֲמֹד / וַיַּעֲצֹר or clean sheva in נָפְלוּ / ונערְמוּ (resh), the fused lower terminal does not independently resolve a vertical pair of sheva dots vs a patah bar or qamats. Retain the vowel disclosure.",
