      "decision": "retainNote",
      "finding": "At zoom6 on viewer page 528, the mark below nun in ונערְמוּ (x=1328..1349, y=891..912) is a single fused asymmetric ink blob with a solid upper horizontal bar (y=891..897) and a right-shifted downward hook (x=1335..1349, y=898..912). Unlike literal nun segol in מִצְנֶפֶת and he/lamed segol in בֵּינֵיהֶם / אֵלֶּה (which show two upper lobes separated by a central top gap plus a centered lower third node), and unlike centered nun qamats in נָסוֹג and נָפְלוּ or flat nun tsere in בֵּינֵיהֶם, the fused contour under nun cannot be certified without grammatical inference. Retain the vowel disclosure.",
